  "decision_summary": "The query is triptolide, a lipophilic diterpenoid triepoxide lactone with poor aqueous solubility and likely extensive first-pass metabolism. The most transferable evidence comes from artemisinin, a structurally related polycyclic lactone natural product with consistently low/poor oral bioavailability, and from 5-hydroxyrofecoxib, a lactone with very low F. Although some unrelated lipophilic natural products (retrorsine, rosaramicin, idarubicin) have F >20%, their structural and mechanistic transferability is weaker. Overall, F <20% is better supported.",
